title: 'pallet-revive: JIT contract execution via sp-virtualization'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Contracts can now be JIT compiled instead of interpreted. The feature is an
    experimental opt-in gated behind the `revive_jit` rustc cfg: runtimes built
    with `--cfg revive_jit` (forwarded into the WASM build by their `build.rs`)
    select the JIT backend at execution time and fall back to the interpreter
    otherwise. Execution is delegated to the node through the pre-existing
    sp-virtualization host functions, backed by a PolkaVM engine running on the
    generic (in-process) sandbox.

    `PristineCode` is now stored as the raw blob (no SCALE length prefix) under
    a manually derived storage key. Weight metering is split per execution
    backend (interpreter/JIT/EVM) with dedicated benchmarks for the JIT
    dispatch and compile-cache costs.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: pallet-revive-proc-macro
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: none
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
